---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import portfolio from '../data/possibilityPortfolio.json';

const active = portfolio.possibilities.filter((item) => item.state === 'active');
const options = portfolio.possibilities.filter((item) => item.state === 'option');
const parked = portfolio.possibilities.filter((item) => item.state === 'parked');
---
<Layout title="Active Frontier" description="The current Agalmic Research commitment set: a deliberately small number of capability-building experiments, with earlier research directions preserved as options rather than obligations.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Possibility portfolio · current commitments</p>
      <h1>Put scarce effort where it can change capability.</h1>
      <p class="lede">The Active Frontier now follows the inward turn of the programme. Ideas and earlier research directions remain preserved, but current substantial effort is attached to real capability needs and real work.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell thesis">
      <p class="eyebrow">Operating rule</p>
      <blockquote>Preserve possibilities cheaply. Commit where the next action can change what you are able to do.</blockquote>
      <p>The portfolio remains an operating aid rather than a validated measure of value. Its role is to stop every interesting branch from silently becoming another obligation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Work-in-progress limit</p>
        <h2>Three substantial bets.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">A fourth exciting idea does not silently become a fourth project.</p>
        <p>The default Active Frontier limit is <strong>{portfolio.wip_limit}</strong>. A new candidate enters when a slot is free, an incumbent leaves, capacity demonstrably increases, or a time-sensitive exception is made explicitly.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Finding prior art, reusing someone else's tool, handing work off or deciding not to pursue a branch can all be successful outcomes.</strong></p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Meta-work budget</p>
        <h2>The scaffolding gets one slot, not the laboratory.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">At most one of the three active bets should primarily concern the machinery, governance, taxonomy or provenance of Agalmic Research itself.</p>
        <p>The other slots should terminate in object-level work: a measured capability change, a working technology under test, an empirical result, a formal result, a reusable intervention, or another outcome constrained by something outside the programme's own vocabulary.</p>
        <p>This is an operating ceiling rather than a metaphysical distinction. If infrastructure becomes the binding constraint on real work, it can earn a slot. It does not earn one merely because the framework can be made more elegant.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Research machinery is justified by the research it makes cheaper, clearer or more falsifiable.</strong></p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Promotion gate</p>
        <h2>Every active bet needs a way to lose.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Before a direction consumes an Active Frontier slot, it should identify the external constraint that can change the decision, the minimum useful test, and the condition under which the claim, mechanism or special terminology would be narrowed, parked or retired.</p>
        <p>“Produce a better explanation” is not enough. A discriminating action should alter belief, capability, architecture, resource allocation or continuation.</p>
        <p><a href="/results/">See results, corrections and retired claims →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Active frontier</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>Where substantial effort is going now.</h2>
          <p>Each active item must have a concrete next action tied to demonstrated capability or learning, not simply more prose.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="index-list">
        {active.map((item, i) => (
          <article class="index-item">
            <span class="index-meta">A{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div>
              <h3>{item.title}</h3>
              <p>{item.summary}</p>
              <p><strong>Intended capability outcome:</strong> {item.worthwhile_future}</p>
              <p><strong>Capacity created:</strong> {item.capacity_created.join(' · ')}</p>
              <p><strong>Next discriminating action:</strong> {item.next_discriminating_action}</p>
              <p class="muted"><strong>Lineage:</strong> {item.lineage_status}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="index-status">active</span>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Frontier filter</p>
        <h2>Capability before novelty.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>A candidate is considered across separate dimensions rather than collapsed into one score: current constraint, capability leverage, information gain, realization or handoff path, attention burden, inheritance already available, urgency and uncertainty.</p>
        <p class="large">The promotion question is: if scarce effort is spent here, what becomes meaningfully easier to understand, judge, create, lead or operate?</p>
        <p>High uncertainty is often a reason to buy information cheaply. High polish is not evidence of learning. Novelty is not required if reuse or implementation produces the needed capability.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Preserved options</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>Worth keeping. Not active obligations.</h2>
          <p>Earlier theory-building directions remain visible and reversible without consuming an Active Frontier slot.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="index-list">
        {options.map((item, i) => (
          <article class="index-item">
            <span class="index-meta">O{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div>
              <h3>{item.title}</h3>
              <p>{item.summary}</p>
              <p><strong>Next discriminating action:</strong> {item.next_discriminating_action}</p>
              <p class="muted"><strong>Lineage:</strong> {item.lineage_status}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="index-status">option</span>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {parked.length > 0 && (
    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="section-number">Parked</span>
          <div class="section-copy">
            <h2>Preserved, but not presently competitive for attention.</h2>
            <p>Parking retains provenance and reversal conditions without pretending every interesting branch deserves current effort.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="index-list">
          {parked.map((item, i) => (
            <article class="index-item">
              <span class="index-meta">P{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <div>
                <h3>{item.title}</h3>
                <p>{item.summary}</p>
                <p><strong>Revisit:</strong> {item.next_discriminating_action}</p>
              </div>
              <span class="index-status">parked</span>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Public boundary</p>
        <h2>This is only the public-safe portfolio.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Confidential, personally sensitive, security-sensitive or potential-IP-sensitive ideas can use the same operating discipline outside the public projection.</p>
        <p>The public JSON projection is versioned at <a href="https://github.com/TsatsuAmable/agalmicresearch/blob/main/src/data/possibilityPortfolio.json">src/data/possibilityPortfolio.json ↗</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
